'The sharper 10-question checklist</h3>\n<ol>\n  <li>What methodology are we using?</li>\n  <li>What is our cadence?</li>\n  <li>What ceremonies do we have — and why?</li>\n  <li>Who owns prioritization?</li>\n  <li>What is our Definition of Done?</li>\n  <li>How do we test and secure the work?</li>\n  <li>How do we deploy and roll back?</li>\n  <li>How do we handle incidents and maintenance?</li>\n  <li>What metrics tell us the process is healthy?</li>\n  <li>How does AI assist or change the process?</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<section class="cite">\n  <strong>Primary sources →</strong>\n  <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_development_process">Software Development Process (Wikipedia)</a> ·\n  <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agile_software_development">Agile Software Development (Wikipedia)</a> ·\n  <a href="https://agilemanifesto.org/">The Agile Manifesto (2001)</a> ·\n  <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scrum_(software_development)">Scrum (Wikipedia)</a> ·\n  <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanban_(development)">Kanban (Wikipedia)</a> ·\n  <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_agent">AI Agent (Wikipedia)</a>\n</section>\n\n<section class="teacher"'